node_modules/

# Transient fixture dirs written by the suites — `module-loader`, `project`,
# `integrations`, `integration-warnings`, `config-cache`, `validate-integration`
# and their successors. They are created and removed per test run, and ignored
# (as upstream ignores its own `.codemod-tsc-*/`) so a crashed run cannot leave
# a stray `.mjs` behind for `prettier --check` and `eslint` to trip over.
#
# One glob rather than a growing list: a new prefix arrives with roughly every
# slice, and the enumerated form had already missed two by the time it was three
# entries long. Nothing real in this package starts with `.astryx-`.
#
# They are repo-local rather than under the OS temp dir purely for parity with
# upstream, whose comment explains it as Vite refusing a dynamic import from
# /tmp. That reason does **not** hold here — an absolute `file://` import from
# the OS temp dir works fine in this setup — so do not repeat it as fact.
.astryx-*/
